[31m│[0m [1minitials returns a string with a lone surrogate                             [0m [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m Every string argument is well formed UTF-16, but the return value contains   [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m an unpaired surrogate (U+D83D at index 0). A lone surrogate renders as a     [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m replacement character, makes encodeURIComponent throw and is changed by      [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m TextEncoder and by JSON round trips through UTF-8. It usually means a string [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m was cut between the two halves of a surrogate pair, for example by slice,    [31m│[0m
[31m│[0m substring, substr or a length limit counted in UTF-16 code units.            [31m│[0m
